@startuml client_send_queue_try_queue_activity
title ClientSendQueue - queued message admission

start
:TryQueue(message, callback);
note right
    Entry: the caller holds lifetime_.mutex_.
    Message-size and lifecycle checks belong to the API caller.
end note
if (pool_ is empty?) then (yes)
    :Return false without reserving a command;
    stop
else (no)
    :Take the front free command;
endif
:Remove the command from pool_;
:Copy message bytes into command.message;
:Move callback into command.callback;
:Append the command to the back of queue_;
:ArmIfNeeded();
:Return true with the caller's lock still held;
stop

legend
    storage_ retains ownership of the command and its message storage.
    Intrusive membership moves from the free pool to the FIFO send queue.
    Admission attempts guarded arming, preserving an occupied reply/drain slot.
    A free slot permits reserving and scheduling dispatch, not immediate transport.
    The API caller validates size/state and turns false into ENOBUFS.
    Empty versus non-empty callback selects SEND versus REQUEST at dispatch.
endlegend

@enduml